<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  THE SWITCH THUMB — Material's own, with ONE state left out.
  ============================================================================

  THE DEFECT. The owner held the IPv6 row down and photographed the switch:
  «зажал ipv6 вкладку, а в переключателе кружочек увеличился, хотя такого быть не
  должно». The thumb had grown to 28dp under a finger that was nowhere near it.

  THE CAUSE IS A PLATFORM RULE AND IT IS WORTH STATING EXACTLY, because the obvious
  fix is the wrong one. ViewGroup.dispatchSetPressed hands the pressed state to its
  children and SKIPS any child that can be pressed on its own:

      if (!pressed || (!child.isClickable() && !child.isLongClickable())) {
          child.setPressed(pressed);
      }

  Every switch in this product is deliberately android:clickable="false" — the WHOLE
  ROW is the one hit target, which is @style/Widget.Departament.Switch's rule and
  view_row.xml's — and that is precisely why it DOES inherit the row's press. M3's
  mtrl_switch_thumb then answers with its state_pressed entry, a 28dp disc, listed
  FIRST so it outranks both checked and unchecked. So the row's press produced a
  second, different response on top of @anim/press_row's, on a control the user was
  not touching.

  Making the switch clickable would stop the dispatch and would also give the row two
  targets that can disagree — the defect five shipped switch rows already had and the
  reason the flag is false in the first place. So the state is refused at the drawable
  instead: this selector simply has no state_pressed entry, a pressed thumb falls
  through to checked or unchecked, and the row's own press response stays the only one.

  NOTHING ELSE IS DROPPED. Both resting sizes (16dp off / 24dp on) and the 250ms
  two-leg morph between them are reproduced from material-1.13.0 exactly — see
  @drawable/switch_thumb_unchecked, _checked and the two transitions, and
  values/tokens_switch_thumb.xml for the paths and durations they share. Copied rather than
  referenced because material's public.txt lists styles only: every mtrl_switch_* is
  private to that library. Colour is untouched and still arrives by tint from
  @color/switch_thumb_selector, as do the track, its decoration ring and the thumb
  icon from their own selectors — none of which has ever had a pressed entry.

  THE ONE THING THAT CHANGES BEYOND THE DEFECT: a switch that IS its own target no
  longer balloons under its own finger either, because a drawable cannot tell whose
  press it is. That is two controls in the product — view_row_line.xml's and
  view_row_card.xml's inline toggles on «Настройки правил маршрутизации» — against
  more than twenty row-owned switches that carried the defect. Consistent, and in the
  direction the owner asked for: this product's switch does not balloon.
-->
<animated-selector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto"
    android:width="@dimen/switch_thumb_size"
    android:height="@dimen/switch_thumb_size">

    <item
        android:id="@+id/switch_thumb_state_checked"
        android:drawable="@drawable/switch_thumb_checked"
        android:state_checked="true" />

    <!-- M3 draws the ON thumb whenever a thumbIcon is present, checked or not, so the
         glyph has a disc big enough to sit in. This app sets no thumbIcon today (only
         thumbIconTint, @color/switch_thumb_icon), so the state never fires — kept so
         that adding one later behaves the way the library does. -->
    <item
        android:id="@+id/switch_thumb_state_with_icon"
        android:drawable="@drawable/switch_thumb_checked"
        app:state_with_icon="true" />

    <item
        android:id="@+id/switch_thumb_state_unchecked"
        android:drawable="@drawable/switch_thumb_unchecked" />

    <transition
        android:drawable="@drawable/switch_thumb_unchecked_checked"
        android:fromId="@+id/switch_thumb_state_unchecked"
        android:toId="@+id/switch_thumb_state_checked" />

    <transition
        android:drawable="@drawable/switch_thumb_unchecked_checked"
        android:fromId="@+id/switch_thumb_state_unchecked"
        android:toId="@+id/switch_thumb_state_with_icon" />

    <transition
        android:drawable="@drawable/switch_thumb_checked_unchecked"
        android:fromId="@+id/switch_thumb_state_checked"
        android:toId="@+id/switch_thumb_state_unchecked" />

    <transition
        android:drawable="@drawable/switch_thumb_checked_unchecked"
        android:fromId="@+id/switch_thumb_state_with_icon"
        android:toId="@+id/switch_thumb_state_unchecked" />

</animated-selector>
